{
  "abstract": "We prove concentration of the realized table of matches in balanced tiered random matching markets under men-proposing deferred acceptance. With fixed finite tier counts, positive population shares a_i and b_j, and fixed positive public scores, every participant independently draws a complete ranking by weighted sampling without replacement. The fraction of all couples joining women's tier i to men's tier j converges in probability to a_i b_j. The theorem allows arbitrary tier-label sequences whose counts differ from n times their prescribed shares by at most one. It proves the exact statement of Formal Conjectures PR 7841, corresponding to Remark H.1 in Tiered Random Matching Markets (2021). The development proves the exponential-arrival representation of the exact profile law, the fixed-woman proposal estimate needed from Proposition G.2 with rounding uniformity, and the independent reference coupling used for concentration.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Bo Cowgill"
    }
  ],
